@startuml rendering-pipeline-flowchart
title Gondwana - Rendering Pipeline (CPU, Desktop GPU, Browser GPU)
' Control flow matches Engine.RunSimulationCycle and DoForegroundTasks.
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #E8F1FF
  BorderColor #4573A8
  ArrowColor #4573A8
}

|Engine simulation / render driver|
start
repeat
  :EngineDispatcher.Drain();
  :Read current tick and delta;
  :RefreshGamepads on hardware cadence;
  :Plugin pre-cycle callback;
  :BeforeBackgroundTasksExecute;
  :PreCycle timers; 
  :Poll keyboard / mouse / touch / gamepad events;
  :Advance tile animations and sprite movement;
  :Resolve collisions for scene layers;
  :Update view cameras;
  :AfterBackgroundTasksExecute;
  if (Foreground render due?) then (yes)
    :Plugin pre-frame callback;
    :BeforeFrameRender;
    :Update Effects for all surfaces;
    :DirectDrawingManager.UpdateAll;
    :Publish desktop GPU RenderFrameSnapshot\nfor eligible surfaces;
    :Render bitmap backbuffers on engine thread;
    :Present bitmap backbuffers via UI adapters;
    :AfterFrameRender (request desktop GPU repaint);
    :PostCycle timers;
    :Plugin post-frame callback;
  endif
  :Update engine FPS / CPS counters as due;
  :Plugin post-cycle callback;
repeat while (Engine running?)
stop

|Desktop GPU paint callback|
start
:Ensure GL backbuffer initialized\n(logical resolution, context, MSAA);
:TryAcquire newest published snapshot;
if (New snapshot available?) then (yes)
  if (Recorded dimensions match?) then (yes)
    :Replay immutable commands to GPU canvas;
    :Flush and snapshot GPU backbuffer;
  else (no)
    :Retain current GPU frame\n(stale logical resolution);
  endif
  :Release mailbox slot;
else (no)
  :Retain current GPU frame;
endif
:Composite GPU backbuffer into platform framebuffer;
:Flush and RecordFrame;
stop

|Blazor bitmap host requestAnimationFrame|
start
:Host.OnAnimationFrame() calls Engine.Tick()\n(StartTimerDriven mode);
:Engine runs due simulation steps and CPU bitmap frames;
:Bitmap UI surface presents latest image;
stop

|Blazor GPU SKGLView paint callback|
start
:Begin paint and ensure GpuBackbuffer initialized;
:Engine.Tick() inside owning SKGLView paint callback;
:Consume foreground frame request;
if (New scene frame needed or backbuffer recreated?) then (yes)
  :Host.GlRenderToCanvas()\nrender scene and present to GPU canvas;
else (no)
  :Host.GlDrawCurrentFrameToCanvas()\nre-present existing GPU frame;
endif
:RecordFrame after successful presentation;
stop

note right
  CPU: dirty-rectangle optimization.
  Desktop GPU: three-slot immutable snapshot mailbox.
  Browser GPU: SKGLView drives Tick, then renders on demand.
  Window resizing and logical resolution are distinct.
end note
@enduml
